<title>USA: UPS Teamsters may return to work Wednesday.</title>
<headline>UPS Teamsters may return to work Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 185,000 Teamsters who are on strike could return to work as soon as Wednesday, a Teamsters spokeswoman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said two representatives from each of the 206 Teamsters locals representing United Parcel Service workers would be invited for an initial vote on the proposed offer at union headquarters in Washington on Tuesday evening.  </p>
<p>The next step, after the Teamsters return to work, would be a vote by all UPS Teamsters on the contract, conducted over the next month, she said.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
</text>
